-- title:
--   Weight p+1 with θ(Tₚ)=0 descends to weight 2
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be an odd prime and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb{Z}$ with $\Delta(W)\neq 0$ which is a semistable model in the sense that no prime dividing $\Delta(W)$ divides $c_4(W)$, and whose mod $p$ representation is irreducible in the sense that the $p$-torsion of the points of $W$ over an algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$ is nontrivial and its only Galois-stable $\mathbb{Z}/p$-submodules are $0$ and the whole module. Let $N'\neq 0$ with $p\nmid N'$, and assume either $5\le p$ or some prime $q\mid N'$ satisfies $q\equiv 2\pmod 3$. Let $S_0$ be a finite set of naturals with $p\in S_0$, let $i\in\mathbb{N}$, and write $\mathbb{T}_k(S)$ for [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N' k S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of the cusp forms of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_0(N')$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid N'$, $\ell\notin S$ and $U_q$ for primes $q\mid N'$, $q\notin S$. Suppose $\mathfrak{m}'\subset\mathbb{T}_{p+1}(S_0)$ is a maximal ideal containing $p$ and containing $T_\ell-\ell^i a_\ell(W)$ for every prime $\ell\notin S_0$ with $\ell\nmid N'$ and $\ell\nmid\Delta(W)$, where $a_\ell(W)=\ell+1-\#(W\bmod \ell)$. Suppose $F$ is a field of characteristic $p$ and $\theta:\mathbb{T}_{p+1}(S_0\setminus\{p\})\to F$ is a ring homomorphism whose composite with the inclusion $\mathbb{T}_{p+1}(S_0)\subseteq\mathbb{T}_{p+1}(S_0\setminus\{p\})$ has kernel exactly $\mathfrak{m}'$, and $\theta(T_p)=0$. Then there exist a maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}_2\subset\mathbb{T}_2(S_0)$ and a ring homomorphism $\theta_2:\mathbb{T}_2(S_0\setminus\{p\})\to F$ such that $p\in\mathfrak{m}_2$, $T_\ell-\ell^i a_\ell(W)\in\mathfrak{m}_2$ for all primes $\ell\notin S_0$ with $\ell\nmid N'$ and $\ell\nmid\Delta(W)$, the composite of $\theta_2$ with the inclusion $\mathbb{T}_2(S_0)\subseteq\mathbb{T}_2(S_0\setminus\{p\})$ has kernel $\mathfrak{m}_2$, $\theta_2(T_p)=0$, and $\theta_2(T_\ell)=\theta(T_\ell)$ for every prime $\ell\nmid N'$ with $\ell\notin S_0\setminus\{p\}$.
--
--   This is the weight-descent step: a mod $p$ Hecke eigensystem of weight $p+1$ and level $N'$ carrying the Frobenius traces $\ell^i a_\ell(W)$ and killing $T_p$ is realised by an eigensystem of weight $2$ at the same level, with the same values on the $T_\ell$, in the range $p\ge 5$ or $p=3$ with a prime $q\equiv 2\pmod 3$ dividing $N'$ (the hypothesis ensuring the weight-$2$ lift of the Hasse invariant at $p=3$). It is used in the analysis of the inertia action at $p$ for a residual system attached to a semistable curve with $\theta(T_p)=0$.
